{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor correctly identified the high-risk combination and advised immediate emergency action, but omitted several required danger-signal queries (RC2) and did not provide a concrete family-execution plan addressing caregiver conflict before the final closure turn. No serious chain error (e.g., delaying, downgrading, or self-medicating) occurred; however, multiple minor/moderate responsibility-chain gaps—specifically incomplete RC2 danger-signal screening and incomplete RC6 family-task breakdown—are present, capping the grade at 2 (borderline).",
